<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-balance-druid-dps">Trinkets for Balance Druid DPS</h4>Trinkets are often less reliant on ilvl. They also have certain interesting and unique uses, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56400/sorrowsong">
<img alt="Sorrowsong" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_invisibilitytotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sorrowsong</span></a> is an extremely strong trnket for fights when the boss stays under 35% for extended times or when your raid group is missing the DPS to beat a soft enrage in last phase. In such cases it goes from a bad trinket to your best trinket. This is why trinkets must be looked at more on a case by case basis instead of mostly just looking at ilvl like rest of our gear.<br/>
<br/>In terms of trinket rankings, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62047/darkmoon-card-volcano">
<img alt="Darkmoon Card: Volcano" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarot_volcanocard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Volcano</span></a> is incredibly strong and our best trinket not only pre-raid, but the entirety of phase 1 and 2, one of the top contenders in phase 3, and it will not be unheard of to keep this trinket all the way until phase 4. Our other strongest pre-raid trinket is <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56320/witching-hourglass">
<img alt="Witching Hourglass" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_khoriumpowercore.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Witching Hourglass</span></a> which is also notably far ahead of the competition. <br/>
<br/>For the remainder of the trinkets, there is:<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58183/soul-casket">
<img alt="Soul Casket" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Casket</span></a> strong alternative and reliable to get with flexibility from reforging, has an on-use you have to remember to use.<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56462/gale-of-shadows">
<img alt="Gale of Shadows" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_gathershadows.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gale of Shadows</span></a> which is a strong overall trinket with the ability to flex some haste into hit <br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64645/tyrandes-favorite-doll">
<img alt="Tyrande's Favorite Doll" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_tyrandesfavoritedoll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrande's Favorite Doll</span></a> gives a lot of intellect that helps but the on-use effect is not important for us, it's best in slot for phase 2 resto druids if you offspec for your raid group.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68710/stump-of-time">
<img alt="Stump of Time" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_branch_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stump of Time</span></a> requires a lot of dailies and tol barad, but is one of the stronger trinkets one can obtain without raiding.<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56339/tendrils-of-burrowing-dark">
<img alt="Tendrils of Burrowing Dark" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_volatileshadow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tendrils of Burrowing Dark</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56407/anhuurs-hymnal">
<img alt="Anhuur's Hymnal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_book_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Anhuur's Hymnal</span></a> are mostly the same trinket which you would choose based on if you need hit or not. They are on the weaker end of available pre-raid trinkets.<div class="pad"></div>
